From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32, kernelbase: file operation progress, Replace or Skip Files

SHFileOperation (copy, move, delete) that takes more than half a second shows
a progress window on its own thread (dlls/shell32/fileopdlg.c): what goes
where, percent, the file in hand, time and items remaining, Cancel. Copying
or moving onto an existing file asks "Replace or Skip Files": replace, skip,
keep both ("name (2).ext"), optionally for all conflicts. kernelbase's
CopyFileEx/CopyFile2 now call their progress routines and honour cancel
flags (they were FIXMEs), which the progress uses.

Gate: test/explorer-gate.sh.
