+/*
+ * SHFileOperation's progress and "Replace or Skip Files" dialogs
+ * (Stained Glass OS)
+ *
+ * A copy, move or delete that takes more than half a second shows how far
+ * it has got -- items, bytes, the file in hand, the time left -- and can be
+ * cancelled, as Windows' does. A copy onto an existing file asks whether to
+ * replace it, skip it or keep both, once or for every conflict.
+ *
+ * The progress window runs on a thread of its own, so it stays responsive
+ * while the operation blocks the caller's thread.
+ *
